/T (Alternative concept and complexity: If all calculations were performed in floating point and rounded only once at the end, intermediate rounding error would be reduced. However, floating-point operations can introduce representation error. Integer-paise arithmetic is deterministic for currency. Both approaches remain O\(1\) per bill because each bill uses a fixed number of arithmetic operations; the main difference is precision and constant-factor cost.)
/E (Alternative concept and complexity: If all calculations were performed in floating point and rounded only once at the end, intermediate rounding error would be reduced. However, floating-point operations can introduce representation error. Integer-paise arithmetic is deterministic for currency. Both approaches remain O\(1\) per bill because each bill uses a fixed number of arithmetic operations; the main difference is precision and constant-factor cost.)
