379 0 obj
<<
/Title (Alternative concept and complexity analysis: If the program were split into input.c, tariff.c, and report.c with a shared header, only the changed source file generally needs recompilation before relinking. In a single-file build, a change to any part causes the whole source file to be recompiled. For a small program the difference is negligible, but for a large project separate compilation can substantially reduce rebuild time. Object files also consume additional disk space, but they enable modular builds and clearer project organisation.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 331 0 R
/Prev 378 0 R
>>
